sequenceDiagram
    participant I1 as Instance 1
    participant I2 as Instance 2
    participant I3 as Instance 3
    participant Lock as Distributed Lock Provider
    participant Anchor as Anchor Store
    
    Note over I1,I3: Job "DailyReport" scheduled via cron (e.g., 0 2 * * *)
    Note over I1,I3: All instances detect it's time to run the job
    
    par Instance 1 attempts
        I1->>Lock: TryAcquire("DailyReport")
        Lock-->>I1: Success (Lock acquired)
    and Instance 2 attempts
        I2->>Lock: TryAcquire("DailyReport")
        Lock-->>I2: Failed (Lock held by I1)
    and Instance 3 attempts
        I3->>Lock: TryAcquire("DailyReport")
        Lock-->>I3: Failed (Lock held by I1)
    end
    
    Note over I1: Instance 1 has the lock
    I1->>Anchor: GetLastRun("DailyReport")
    Anchor-->>I1: 2024-01-04 02:00:00
    
    Note over I1: Checks if job should run based on cron and last run
    alt Job should run
        I1->>I1: Execute Job Logic
        I1->>Anchor: UpdateLastRun("DailyReport", now)
        Note over I1: Job completed successfully
    else Job already ran (anchor recent)
        Note over I1: Skip execution - another instance already ran it
    end
    
    I1->>Lock: Release("DailyReport")
    
    Note over I2,I3: Failed instances wait and retry
    
    I2->>Lock: TryAcquire("DailyReport") (after delay)
    Lock-->>I2: Success (I1 released the lock)
    
    I2->>Anchor: GetLastRun("DailyReport")
    Anchor-->>I2: 2024-01-04 02:00:00 (updated by I1)
    
    Note over I2: Sees job already executed - anchor is recent
    I2->>Lock: Release("DailyReport")
    
    Note over I1,I3: All instances now wait for next scheduled time
    Note over I1,I3: Process repeats - any instance can win the lock